Adaptations:
- Preserve the native singleton tmpfs, device_get_devnode naming, modes, ownership,
  synchronous worker requests, kernel-node markers and deletion semantics.
- Late loading uses a private fs_struct/root instead of boot-only init_mount/chroot.
- The worker retains the authorized loader's credentials for VFS operations;
  no SELinux policy is changed, and it never runs a userspace command.
- Validate device_add/device_del prologues before permanent entry replacements.
- Enumerate existing device kobjects with references, excluding registrations or
  deletions in progress. Serialize node updates without holding our mutex across
  driver core callbacks, which may recursively unregister child devices.
- Device creation/deletion hooks remain pinned until reboot; report errors and
  initialization readiness through read-only module parameters.
- Restrict loading to the recorded PLZ110 / canoe kernel and its test kernels.
